        "summary":  "The Global Leadership Scholarship is a tuition fee discount of GBP 10,000 from the University of Glasgow for International and EU fee students starting a full-time, one-year, in-person taught Master\u0027s in any discipline in September 2027 (academic session 2027/2028). There are 350 awards. Applicants need grades equivalent to UK first class honours and an offer of a place. The discount applies to one year only.",
        "eligibility_notes":  "You must have International or EU fee status and hold an offer of a place for a full-time one-year Master\u0027s programme starting September 2027.\n\nYou must show academic excellence, with grades equivalent to UK first class honours. The page does not give a country-by-country grade conversion; the scholarship FAQ says eligibility varies and points applicants who are unsure to the criteria or to the university.\n\nOnly one-year, full-time, in-person Master\u0027s programmes qualify. Diplomas and certificates are not eligible. Book and Paper Conservation MPhil and Textile Conservation MPhil are also eligible, with the discount applied to the first year only.\n\nThe page carries an \u0027Eligible countries/regions\u0027 list of about 190 countries and territories; it does not say whether this refers to nationality, residence or fee status, and the United Kingdom is not on it.\n\nYou cannot hold more than one University of Glasgow discount or scholarship, and they cannot be combined with external partnership discounts. The only exception is the Alumni Discount. If you are offered more than one, the lower value award is removed from your account.\n\nYour offer conditions, including English language requirements, do not affect how the scholarship application is assessed. You do not need an offer to apply for a scholarship, but you need a submitted programme application.",
        "age_experience_notes":  "",
        "funding_summary":  "A GBP 10,000 tuition fee waiver, given as a tuition fee discount for one year only. No other cost is described as covered.",
        "programmes_note":  "Any discipline, as long as the programme is a one-year, full-time, in-person Master\u0027s on the published eligible list (the list spans arts, business, engineering, law, medicine, science, social sciences and education, and includes MBA and some Dumfries campus programmes). Diplomas and certificates are not eligible. The full list is on the scholarship page.",
        "institutions_note":  "University of Glasgow only, including its Dumfries campus for the programmes marked so on the list.",
